{"name":"Paula Loves Paris","hex":"#80a4cd","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"loves","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of love"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["third-person singular simple present indicative of love"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/loves"},{"term":"paris","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of pari."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/paris"}],"entries":[{"title":"Love's","blocks":[{"text":"Love's Travel Stops, doing business as Love's, is an American family owned-and-operated chain of more than 670 travel stops in 42 states in the United States. The company is privately owned and headquartered in Oklahoma City. Love's ranked No. 15 on the 2025 Forbes list of America's largest private companies. Love's has two primary kinds of stores: country stores and travel stops. Country stores are fueling stations with a convenience store attached. The larger travel stops are located along highways and offer additional amenities such as food from restaurant chains such as Arby's, Bojangles, Burger King, Chester's, Dunkin' Donuts, McDonald's, Taco John's, Subway, Wendy's, Hardee's/Carl's Jr., truck parking spaces, showers and laundry. The company started adding RV hookups and RV Stops in 2022. Love's had more than 40,000 employees in 2023."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1d/Love%27s_Travel_Stop_%28Bushnell%2C_Fla.%29_%2849417678437%29.jpg/330px-Love%27s_Travel_Stop_%28Bushnell%2C_Fla.%29_%2849417678437%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Love's","wikidata":"Q1872496"},{"title":"Paris","blocks":[{"text":"Paris is the capital and largest city of France, with an estimated city population of 2.04 million in an area of 105.4 km2 (40.7 sq mi), as of January 2026, and a metropolitan population of 13.3 million (2023). Located on the Seine in the centre of the Île-de-France region, it is the largest metropolitan area and fourth-most populous city in the European Union (EU). Paris is nicknamed the \"City of Light\" mainly due to its leading role in the Age of Enlightenment."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4b/La_Tour_Eiffel_vue_de_la_Tour_Saint-Jacques%2C_Paris_ao%C3%BBt_2014_%282%29.jpg/330px-La_Tour_Eiffel_vue_de_la_Tour_Saint-Jacques%2C_Paris_ao%C3%BBt_2014_%282%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paris","wikidata":"Q90"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/28/Love%27s_in_Choctaw.jpg/500px-Love%27s_in_Choctaw.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/28/Love%27s_in_Choctaw.jpg/1280px-Love%27s_in_Choctaw.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/28/Love%27s_in_Choctaw.jpg/500px-Love%27s_in_Choctaw.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Love's Travel Stops fuel island off Interstate 40 in Choctaw, Oklahoma","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALove's_in_Choctaw.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c4/Love%27s_gas_station.jpg/500px-Love%27s_gas_station.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c4/Love%27s_gas_station.jpg/1280px-Love%27s_gas_station.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c4/Love%27s_gas_station.jpg/500px-Love%27s_gas_station.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Love's Travel Stops off I-90/I-94 in Oakdale, Wisconsin","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALove's_gas_